{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/80710-archmastery-sub-souls-and-soul-pacts","id":80710,"title":"Archmastery, Sub-souls, and Soul Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-26T19:18:10-08:00","id":80710,"title":"Archmastery, Sub-souls, and Soul Pacts","content":"So it recently came up in the planning steps of a game, and I wasn't sure what to tell the players. What would happen if a Demon successfully managed to make a soul pact with an Archmaster's sub-soul? I have an idea of what happens on the Demons end (not much, I don't think Archmaster souls can be removed/destroyed, unless I'm wrong), but what happens to the Arch Master? <br /> <br /> Are they just not allowed to make such a pact? Would either know this? (And is there any support in the books for your ideas? I'm still haven't finished my cover-to-cover read through)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2382-krimcl","name":"krimcl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:19:59-08:00","id":80711,"title":"","content":"Also semi relevant, if a Mage turns say... A rabbit into a human, then places an actual soul in it AND raises its intelligence... Is it capable of making a soul pact? If so, how much cover would that be worth? Would it be broken at the end of the spells duration? How much Legend does a rabbit provide? A deep love of carrots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2382-krimcl","name":"krimcl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:44:57-08:00","id":80728,"title":"","content":"I would probably not have a situation like that arise if I were running Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T21:07:49-08:00","id":80777,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind that Archmastery is tier 4 game... while other games are tier 3 at the highest, given the materials at hand. So like Caladriu, I would not have the possibility to run into that sort of problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T21:28:03-08:00","id":80792,"title":"","content":"Archmasters are tier 4, yes. But their sub souls do exist in the world, and despite the Pax, it is made quite clear they do have a presence in the fallen world, that is, in fact almost entirely what sub souls are for.<br /> And if Demons can't ever deal with /anything/ involved with a Tier 4 game/entity then a world free from the God Machine (which seems to be the most common version of Hell in some fashion or another) is absolutely impossible, as that appears to be the scale the God Machine exists on... Which makes the entire point of Decent... Pointless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2382-krimcl","name":"krimcl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T21:42:02-08:00","id":80796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>krimcl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/80710-archmastery-sub-souls-and-soul-pacts#post80710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it recently came up in the planning steps of a game, and I wasn't sure what to tell the players. What would happen if a Demon successfully managed to make a soul pact with an Archmaster's sub-soul? I have an idea of what happens on the Demons end (not much, I don't think Archmaster souls can be removed/destroyed, unless I'm wrong), but what happens to the Arch Master?<br /> <br /> Are they just not allowed to make such a pact? Would either know this? (And is there any support in the books for your ideas? I'm still haven't finished my cover-to-cover read through)</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, A subsoul has no control over a soul. while they can die. They are still part of the archmaster. They'd still be soul immune. The pact wouldn't go through. But you are the ST. If you wanted to make it happen you could. The archmaster would know something was up though and deal with the demon as he cost him a more likely than not powerful servant. The demon wouldn't really be able to fool the archmaster because of the innate connection between them that the demon can't replicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T00:20:30-08:00","id":80857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>krimcl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/80710-archmastery-sub-souls-and-soul-pacts?p=80711#post80711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also semi relevant, if a Mage turns say... A rabbit into a human, then places an actual soul in it AND raises its intelligence... Is it capable of making a soul pact? If so, how much cover would that be worth? Would it be broken at the end of the spells duration? How much Legend does a rabbit provide? A deep love of carrots?</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to have some of your players checked into a mental ward...<br /> <br /> When you start parsing rules to this degree it all becomes subjective to the point where you have to just decide what to do. Is there a right call here? Likely not. There's a bit of a debate on whether humans are in someway 'special' inherently or if it's just physiology that causes the difference, so your stance on that is going to influence your decision here. That being said, I'll give you my personal insights to consider, as that seems to be what you've come here for:<br /> <br /> What is it that makes a human special over an animal? Their brains and their bodies. All creatures have a soul and I really don't think us humans have an inherently 'special' one. So if you overcome those limitations via magic a soul pact should be possible, but only so long as the magic persists. But for this crazy hybrid-rabbit to sign a Soul Pact it will need to understand spoken and written language (not that you should tell your players that). I don't know off-hand if there's a spell for that but an alternative could be to use Animal Communication to talk to this.... human (this is getting weird). You'd still have to convince them to sign a Contract but that's likely to be laughably easy.<br /> <br /> How much Cover? Consider the source of your Cover. Normally it's the ability of the identity to blend in with the world. With this person just appearing out of nowhere with no back story, no friends, no family, no name, not even any clothes. I'd grant the lowest rating possible of 1 which would make avoiding compromises nearly impossible. Maybe the agents of the God Machine sense this unholy abomination coming into creation, it's up to you.<br /> <br /> What would happen when the duration ends? My take is that it's the human's ability to understand their Contract that allow the demon to possess their soul so a lowly rabbit would reject them. Maybe this happens in public and they expose their demonic form, it's up to you.<br /> <br /> Haha, so for legend on a rabbit? I'd say Animal Ken, Survival and Stealth make sense. Maybe Athletics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2390-yolo420swag","name":"#yolo420swag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2390_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T10:43:40-08:00","id":81128,"title":"","content":"Epimetheus and #yolo420swag <br /> Thanks for helping to answer my (admittedly crazy) situational questions.<br /> That said, as a Mage investigating the nature of the soul, or a demon maybe doing the same, the situation would provide an interesting insight into the metaphysics of the world and the soul, even if it just raised more questions.<br /> And by typing that and rereading I know think that maybe institutionalization isn't the worst idea for someone suggesting such experiments....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2382-krimcl","name":"krimcl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T12:10:55-08:00","id":81158,"title":"","content":"The soul pact wouldn't form, nothing would happen to the sub-soul, and what kind of game are you playing, anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T15:10:48-08:00","id":81257,"title":"","content":"A cross over game where I let the players pick from any template. The plot is involving the Prince of 100,000 Leaves. And I probably gave out /way/ too much XP to start with. (under the GMC rules 60 to each player).<br /> The players consist of 2 Mages, 2 Demons, A hunter, A vampire, and a were-elephant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2382-krimcl","name":"krimcl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T15:36:23-08:00","id":81275,"title":"","content":"Cool!<br /> <br /> Well, while it'd be a surprise to a Demon to learn that his intended mark didn't have a normal soul but instead shared one in a bizarre cosmic hierarchy, it might come as even more of a surprise to the sub-soul in question - archmages don't always grant their avatars the knowledge that they <i>are</i> avatars. The archmage would likely notice the Pacting attempt, though. Lots of plot hooks there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T08:14:37-08:00","id":81600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>#yolo420swag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/80710-archmastery-sub-souls-and-soul-pacts?p=80857#post80857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Their brains and their bodies. All creatures have a soul and I really don't think us humans have an inherently 'special' one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idle curiosity, but could one turn an animal into a Revenant (requires a soul)? Could a Demon make a Soul Pact with a human revenant? (as Revenants are souls bound to a body)<br /> <br /> (Mostly, I just want to make sharks into revenants and give them a Numina that allows them to swim through earth and stone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T09:19:16-08:00","id":81628,"title":"","content":"The whole thing of &quot;animals have a soul&quot; is up to debate. In real life, in game, you name it. So, the answer is always, &quot;whatever your ST says.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T18:28:35-08:00","id":81854,"title":"","content":"<br /> One thing to note, whether or not animals have souls by default, there's not going to be much that'll stop a powerful enough spirit mage from taking someone's soul and attaching it to an animal, besides this being insane anyway. But a Demon is not going to want to pact a weird magical animal-human hybrid for the same reason it's not going to want to pact a vampire or werewolf. The point of cover is to stay hidden, not attract attention to oneself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T18:34:23-08:00","id":81856,"title":"","content":"On a random note, what happens when you try making a pact with a familiar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}